(2770087, 383043, 42100, '<td valign="top">Very moody landscape, I really like the low key lighting.  Great job!</td>', 'Very moody landscape, I really like the low key lighting.  Great job!', '2006-08-29 10:36:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770095, 383616, 42100, '<td valign="top">Very beautiful scenic, that setting sun lighting is very cool.  Makes for a really smooth and tranquil photograph.  Gorgeous!</td>', 'Very beautiful scenic, that setting sun lighting is very cool.  Makes for a really smooth and tranquil photograph.  Gorgeous!', '2006-08-29 10:38:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770114, 383938, 5792, '<td valign="top">A very different interpretation of the challenge topic. This is a good metaphoric representation of someone wandering lost and bonded closely to nature in order to get through it and find their way back. Like the use of the rule of thirds for representing "The Lost Photographer" but unsure how well the border fits the image.<br/> I wished to have corn to eat out where I was lost. That would have been tastier than the sprouts and cactus fruit I ate. It is interesting to note that in this area (Phoenix, Arizona USA), where irrigated, corn is grown in abundance and looks just like this. Next time I think I''ll choose to get lost there. :) - Steve</td>', 'A very different interpretation of the challenge topic. This is a good metaphoric representation of someone wandering lost and bonded closely to nature in order to get through it and find their way back. Like the use of the rule of thirds for representing "The Lost Photographer" but unsure how well the border fits the image. I wished to have corn to eat out where I was lost. That would have been tastier than the sprouts and cactus fruit I ate. It is interesting to note that in this area (Phoenix, Arizona USA), where irrigated, corn is grown in abundance and looks just like this. Next time I think I''ll choose to get lost there. :) - Steve', '2006-08-29 10:46:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770116, 383616, 5792, '<td valign="top">Nice color and light processing that adds body and depth to the composition. The exceptionally clean look and clarity makes this image good. The greens are great and compliment the lavenders, blues and reds of the sky. The image has an almost surrealistic look to it. Decent technical quality. The people look as though they are searchng for "the lost photographer".<br/> Personally, I would rather have been lost at the beach with a cooler full of beer than with nothing in the desert. Think I''ll try it that way next time. LOL! My sister and niece put up flyers along the Oregon coast near one of my favorite beaches there in an attempt to relocate me. - Steve</td>', 'Nice color and light processing that adds body and depth to the composition. The exceptionally clean look and clarity makes this image good. The greens are great and compliment the lavenders, blues and reds of the sky. The image has an almost surrealistic look to it. Decent technical quality. The people look as though they are searchng for "the lost photographer". Personally, I would rather have been lost at the beach with a cooler full of beer than with nothing in the desert. Think I''ll try it that way next time. LOL! My sister and niece put up flyers along the Oregon coast near one of my favorite beaches there in an attempt to relocate me. - Steve', '2006-08-29 10:46:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770121, 384131, 5792, '<td valign="top">Unsure exactly what it all really means, but very creative. I''ll try most anything once. :) Good general technical quality and the white background fits. (I think). There is only a bit of haloing around the girl gorilla''s foot. Colors work and the way the she is holding the photographer down in the trunk is cute. Balance and composition are fine. Nicely done.<br/> Some thoughts that come to my mind regarding the meaning of this image are a lot scarier than others, if you get my drift. They make being lost in the desert seem tame. LOL! However, The frog prince is my DPC profile picture. That is because I''m still waiting for waiting for a beautiful princess to kiss me and turn me back into a handsome prince. If you are lovely maiden cloaked in a gorilla looking for a handsome prince to return you to your true self then we need to talk more. If not, then I am running back out into the desert as fast as I can. - Steve</td>', 'Unsure exactly what it all really means, but very creative. I''ll try most anything once. :) Good general technical quality and the white background fits. (I think). There is only a bit of haloing around the girl gorilla''s foot. Colors work and the way the she is holding the photographer down in the trunk is cute. Balance and composition are fine. Nicely done. Some thoughts that come to my mind regarding the meaning of this image are a lot scarier than others, if you get my drift. They make being lost in the desert seem tame. LOL! However, The frog prince is my DPC profile picture. That is because I''m still waiting for waiting for a beautiful princess to kiss me and turn me back into a handsome prince. If you are lovely maiden cloaked in a gorilla looking for a handsome prince to return you to your true self then we need to talk more. If not, then I am running back out into the desert as fast as I can. - Steve', '2006-08-29 10:48:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770125, 384055, 5792, '<td valign="top">A very nice tribute to "Sonoran Spring", even the clouds look right. Appears like it was shot with a polarizer filter like the original. Nicely done B&amp;W with excellent tonality, especially in the clouds and sky. Beautifully captured.<br/> Oddly enough, this scene is reasonably close to what it looked like where I was actually lost. Cactus were not quite as nice where I was at, though, but the low hills were similar. "Sonoran Spring" was shot on the opposite side of the Superstition Mountains from where I got lost.<br/> During my trek I saw towering thunderhead clouds that made for absolutely spectacular sunsets. Sunrises were beautiful to, but alas... So sad... no pictures. :( - Steve</td>', 'A very nice tribute to "Sonoran Spring", even the clouds look right. Appears like it was shot with a polarizer filter like the original. Nicely done B&W with excellent tonality, especially in the clouds and sky. Beautifully captured. Oddly enough, this scene is reasonably close to what it looked like where I was actually lost. Cactus were not quite as nice where I was at, though, but the low hills were similar. "Sonoran Spring" was shot on the opposite side of the Superstition Mountains from where I got lost. During my trek I saw towering thunderhead clouds that made for absolutely spectacular sunsets. Sunrises were beautiful to, but alas... So sad... no pictures. :( - Steve', '2006-08-29 10:50:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770128, 382999, 5792, '<td valign="top">Nice interplay of lavender and orangish color tones to make a very appealing image. There is just something about bridges that will always fascinate the viewer. Very clean image, nicely post processed with excellent sharpness.<br/> I tell ya, I''d rather have been stranded in NYC''s concrete jungle than the hot Sonoran desert... Beer is a lot closer in NYC. Think I''ll try losing myself your way next time. Doubt I''d be easier to find, though. ;) - Steve</td>', 'Nice interplay of lavender and orangish color tones to make a very appealing image. There is just something about bridges that will always fascinate the viewer. Very clean image, nicely post processed with excellent sharpness. I tell ya, I''d rather have been stranded in NYC''s concrete jungle than the hot Sonoran desert... Beer is a lot closer in NYC. Think I''ll try losing myself your way next time. Doubt I''d be easier to find, though. ;) - Steve', '2006-08-29 10:51:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770134, 383749, 5792, '<td valign="top">Good general technical image quality. Like the sepia. Since the boat and the bridge support are the items that attract the most viewer attention I would like to have see them take up more image real estate, perhaps try centering the bridge support along the upper left rule of thirds intersection point and the boat aligned on the lower right rule of thirds intersection point.<br/> I can tell you this, I felt like I was about three sheets to the wind for a lot of the time I was missing. ;) Creative interpretation of the challenge topic. - Steve</td>', 'Good general technical image quality. Like the sepia. Since the boat and the bridge support are the items that attract the most viewer attention I would like to have see them take up more image real estate, perhaps try centering the bridge support along the upper left rule of thirds intersection point and the boat aligned on the lower right rule of thirds intersection point. I can tell you this, I felt like I was about three sheets to the wind for a lot of the time I was missing. ;) Creative interpretation of the challenge topic. - Steve', '2006-08-29 10:53:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770152, 383845, 5792, '<td valign="top">Very, very creative idea. Like it lot. Use of the light shining up out of the box is a great idea. This is a tricky shot to pull off. The concept is fantastic but the technical execution could be a little better. The brightness from the boxlight overexposes your upper body and face a bit to much and hifting the center of focus to your face might work a little better. You are getting some reddish/yellowish color overtones on the arms and hair, but there is a way with curves and/or Hue Saturation to shift it back to natural colors. Pull me out of that box and I''ll show you how to fix that with Photoshop. :)<br/> Be careful removing me, though, and keep that outreaching hand under control. After all, I''ve been ALONE in the desert for a long, long time... hard telling what I might latch on to, if you know what I mean. LOL!!! You can rescue me any time! - Steve</td>', 'Very, very creative idea. Like it lot. Use of the light shining up out of the box is a great idea. This is a tricky shot to pull off. The concept is fantastic but the technical execution could be a little better. The brightness from the boxlight overexposes your upper body and face a bit to much and hifting the center of focus to your face might work a little better. You are getting some reddish/yellowish color overtones on the arms and hair, but there is a way with curves and/or Hue Saturation to shift it back to natural colors. Pull me out of that box and I''ll show you how to fix that with Photoshop. :) Be careful removing me, though, and keep that outreaching hand under control. After all, I''ve been ALONE in the desert for a long, long time... hard telling what I might latch on to, if you know what I mean. LOL!!! You can rescue me any time! - Steve', '2006-08-29 11:03:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770160, 383343, 5792, '<td valign="top">Beautifully done, nice time exposure capture and good technical quality and sharpness. The smoky bluish background is nice. The starburst light on the left and the foreground silhouette add viewer interest to the composition. This image should place very high in voting.<br/> Sometimes I felt like I was sucked into a vortex while I was lost. If it would have been here at least I could have said I got dizzy and that is why I could not find my way back out again. :) - Steve</td>', 'Beautifully done, nice time exposure capture and good technical quality and sharpness. The smoky bluish background is nice. The starburst light on the left and the foreground silhouette add viewer interest to the composition. This image should place very high in voting. Sometimes I felt like I was sucked into a vortex while I was lost. If it would have been here at least I could have said I got dizzy and that is why I could not find my way back out again. :) - Steve', '2006-08-29 11:06:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770162, 382463, 5792, '<td valign="top">OhhhhhK! Believe me, I wonder to. :) I can tell you this, those beans and peas would have tasted mighty good when I was lost in the desert. Getting the can open would have been a trick but I''d have figured out something.<br/> Btw, Elvis stopped in to see how I was doing during my delirious desert wanderings. I can accurately report that he is alive and well. Can''t quite put my finger on it but your depiction of Elvis has never made him look better. ;) - Steve</td>', 'OhhhhhK! Believe me, I wonder to. :) I can tell you this, those beans and peas would have tasted mighty good when I was lost in the desert. Getting the can open would have been a trick but I''d have figured out something. Btw, Elvis stopped in to see how I was doing during my delirious desert wanderings. I can accurately report that he is alive and well. Can''t quite put my finger on it but your depiction of Elvis has never made him look better. ;) - Steve', '2006-08-29 11:07:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770168, 382660, 5792, '<td valign="top">"Incognito" describes well my experience being lost. This is a nice, cute  composition. Wish the experience would have been as whimsical as this depiction. Soft focused background highlights the main subject well. I was hidden in amongst desert plants so this is an appropriate image describing where I might be, the plants just need to be thornier. :) - Steve</td>', '"Incognito" describes well my experience being lost. This is a nice, cute  composition. Wish the experience would have been as whimsical as this depiction. Soft focused background highlights the main subject well. I was hidden in amongst desert plants so this is an appropriate image describing where I might be, the plants just need to be thornier. :) - Steve', '2006-08-29 11:08:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770241, 383996, 42100, '<td valign="top">A really desolate looking setting, kind of cold and dismal looking as well.  Very nice!</td>', 'A really desolate looking setting, kind of cold and dismal looking as well.  Very nice!', '2006-08-29 11:52:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770243, 383358, 42100, '<td valign="top">A very interesting silhouette and fantastic sky colors.  Great job!</td>', 'A very interesting silhouette and fantastic sky colors.  Great job!', '2006-08-29 11:53:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770291, 383241, 27482, '<td valign="top">Nice shot, can´t really see what it has to do with the challenge itself with the current title, can´t make out a pond house and my personal opinion on this shot is that you shoehorned it into this challenge by using a title but so what...  Nice enough shot, gave it a 6.</td>', 'Nice shot, can´t really see what it has to do with the challenge itself with the current title, can´t make out a pond house and my personal opinion on this shot is that you shoehorned it into this challenge by using a title but so what...  Nice enough shot, gave it a 6.', '2006-08-29 12:09:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770294, 383337, 27482, '<td valign="top">Nice shot, think I would have liked it more though with a wider shot, composition feels a little cramped to me.  6 from me</td>', 'Nice shot, think I would have liked it more though with a wider shot, composition feels a little cramped to me.  6 from me', '2006-08-29 12:09:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770295, 384185, 27482, '<td valign="top">Nice shot, I think I would have liked it better though with a stronger contrast, feels a little flat to me.</td>', 'Nice shot, I think I would have liked it better though with a stronger contrast, feels a little flat to me.', '2006-08-29 12:10:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770299, 384060, 27482, '<td valign="top">Almost missed that guy (wich I assume is you) and can imagine a lot of others are doing that and your score is suffering.  Image seems a little dark but nothing serious and nothing that hurts it in my opinion.  6 from me.</td>', 'Almost missed that guy (wich I assume is you) and can imagine a lot of others are doing that and your score is suffering.  Image seems a little dark but nothing serious and nothing that hurts it in my opinion.  6 from me.', '2006-08-29 12:11:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770301, 383616, 27482, '<td valign="top">Lovely color composition and composition in general, gave it a 7.</td>', 'Lovely color composition and composition in general, gave it a 7.', '2006-08-29 12:11:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770307, 383343, 27482, '<td valign="top">I like this shot but not really the vantage point it´s shot from, those two signs infront are really only drawing my eye away from the "vortex" and so is that lightflare up in the left corner.  Still really like it and gave this shot a 7 but would potentially had been a 10 and a favorite if you had used a wider lens, gotten in more close behind the signs and pretty much had only the "vortex", possibly shot more from the ground up?</td>', 'I like this shot but not really the vantage point it´s shot from, those two signs infront are really only drawing my eye away from the "vortex" and so is that lightflare up in the left corner.  Still really like it and gave this shot a 7 but would potentially had been a 10 and a favorite if you had used a wider lens, gotten in more close behind the signs and pretty much had only the "vortex", possibly shot more from the ground up?', '2006-08-29 12:13:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770309, 383973, 27482, '<td valign="top">Pheew, he must smell really bad then :)</td>', 'Pheew, he must smell really bad then :)', '2006-08-29 12:13:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770315, 383845, 27482, '<td valign="top">Love the idea, just not as fond of the lighting, think I would have liked this image better if the light coming out of the box were not as intense, less of it and more soft and had some slight more ambient lighting for the surroundings.  Keep at it, this idea is promising.</td>', 'Love the idea, just not as fond of the lighting, think I would have liked this image better if the light coming out of the box were not as intense, less of it and more soft and had some slight more ambient lighting for the surroundings.  Keep at it, this idea is promising.', '2006-08-29 12:15:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770319, 382988, 27482, '<td valign="top">The composition gives me a slight sense of vertigo, very unpleasant really, I think I would have liked this a lot better if you had turned about 15 degrees clockwise when taking this photo.  Like the idea, 6 from me.</td>', 'The composition gives me a slight sense of vertigo, very unpleasant really, I think I would have liked this a lot better if you had turned about 15 degrees clockwise when taking this photo.  Like the idea, 6 from me.', '2006-08-29 12:17:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2770327, 383252, 27482, '<td valign="top">Nice shot but would have been ace if you had someone standing in that doorway maybe with his back turned to us or maybe peeking out of the dooway? Would have been more in the spirit of the challenge, in my opinion ofcourse.</td>', 'Nice shot but would have been ace if you had someone standing in that doorway maybe with his back turned to us or maybe peeking out of the dooway? Would have been more in the spirit of the challenge, in my opinion ofcourse.', '2006-08-29 12:18:27.000000', NULL, 1),
