(2772550, 383616, 48228, '<td valign="top">Now Robert, you are the man, and I love this one mate..... <br/>It would also be a great example for the next up-coming challenge, re "Pastels".....<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-08-30 01:11:07.</i></td>', 'Now Robert, you are the man, and I love this one mate..... It would also be a great example for the next up-coming challenge, re "Pastels".....', '2006-08-30 02:10:39.000000', '2006-08-30 02:11:07.000000', 0),
(2772557, 383358, 5792, '<td valign="top">Wow! Congratulations on your first ribbon and first 7+ score!!!!!<br/> <br/>What an amazing story! I can''t believe you drove all the way from Riverside to the Supertitions. Sounds like you had a great time. Wished I could have shared it with you. While "missing" one of the trails I hiked on was the Siphon''s Draw trail!</td>', 'Wow! Congratulations on your first ribbon and first 7+ score!!!!! What an amazing story! I can''t believe you drove all the way from Riverside to the Supertitions. Sounds like you had a great time. Wished I could have shared it with you. While "missing" one of the trails I hiked on was the Siphon''s Draw trail!', '2006-08-30 02:11:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2772574, 383910, 39880, '<td valign="top">Great perspective.  I like how the orange lines really stand out.</td>', 'Great perspective.  I like how the orange lines really stand out.', '2006-08-30 02:12:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2772575, 384091, 23430, '<td valign="top">Great image. Attention to detail, composition and lighting are all great. Funny as well. Congrats on your BLUE.</td>', 'Great image. Attention to detail, composition and lighting are all great. Funny as well. Congrats on your BLUE.', '2006-08-30 02:12:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2772578, 383738, 48228, '<td valign="top">Yes, I really like this one, and well done on this fine finish.....</td>', 'Yes, I really like this one, and well done on this fine finish.....', '2006-08-30 02:13:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2772653, 384195, 5792, '<td valign="top">Great job! Congratulations of the red ribbon.<br/> <br/>Gee... You got naked just for little ol'' me? Why couldn''t some of the DPC girls do that? LOL!!!<br/> <br/>Great job... great photo... well deserved ribbon.</td>', 'Great job! Congratulations of the red ribbon. Gee... You got naked just for little ol'' me? Why couldn''t some of the DPC girls do that? LOL!!! Great job... great photo... well deserved ribbon.', '2006-08-30 02:24:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2772747, 383904, 31133, '<td valign="top">Gugi, I think you really need more than just two comments on this shot! At first, I thought the guy was a Ken doll, not a real person. Too bad about the shadows on his face, but probably wasn''t the best opportunity to use fill flash. I love, love, love his black &amp; white feathers! (not so crazy about the pink ones, unless he had all pink feathers - but that''s neither here nor there). When I first saw this, I think my mind was set on that Steve was at some place - so I didn''t really make the connection to the entry, being as how my head was stuck in landscapes. Now I see that the idea is that Steve is partying, which I think (now) is a great idea! It''s a fun take on the challenge. I didn''t score this very high to be honest. If the detail in the man had been as strong as it is in the clouds, it would''ve boosted my score. Hope you don''t mind my comments. You know you''re one of my favorite photographers in the whole world.</td>', 'Gugi, I think you really need more than just two comments on this shot! At first, I thought the guy was a Ken doll, not a real person. Too bad about the shadows on his face, but probably wasn''t the best opportunity to use fill flash. I love, love, love his black & white feathers! (not so crazy about the pink ones, unless he had all pink feathers - but that''s neither here nor there). When I first saw this, I think my mind was set on that Steve was at some place - so I didn''t really make the connection to the entry, being as how my head was stuck in landscapes. Now I see that the idea is that Steve is partying, which I think (now) is a great idea! It''s a fun take on the challenge. I didn''t score this very high to be honest. If the detail in the man had been as strong as it is in the clouds, it would''ve boosted my score. Hope you don''t mind my comments. You know you''re one of my favorite photographers in the whole world.', '2006-08-30 02:41:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2772815, 383853, 50674, '<td valign="top">I thought it might be you when I saw the bridge. Well done Amy!</td>', 'I thought it might be you when I saw the bridge. Well done Amy!', '2006-08-30 02:59:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2772830, 383904, 50674, '<td valign="top">Thank you.<br/>I have been grinning all week - one little comment apart from Steve''s comment. Well, sometimes the dpc-ers just live up to their reputation.<br/>Someone here has this signature: "I want to thank the narrow people for clarifying what''s really important." Wish I had written that :)<br/>That same person also says: "Be an artist, not a score whore" (Had to come back and edit, had not gotten that last one right.)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-09-03 06:05:06.</i></td>', 'Thank you.I have been grinning all week - one little comment apart from Steve''s comment. Well, sometimes the dpc-ers just live up to their reputation.Someone here has this signature: "I want to thank the narrow people for clarifying what''s really important." Wish I had written that :)That same person also says: "Be an artist, not a score whore" (Had to come back and edit, had not gotten that last one right.)', '2006-08-30 03:06:08.000000', '2006-09-03 07:05:06.000000', 0),
